    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n930" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad-murmŭro</span></b> , āvi,
			ātum, 1, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to murmur with approbation</i> or
				<i>disapprobation</i> (cf. acclamo): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quam valde universi admurmurārint,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Verr. 2, 5, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">admurmurante senatu neque me invito,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 1, 13, 2</span></i>
			.—<i>Impers.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum esset admurmuratum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. de Or. 2, 70, 285</span></i>
			.</div>
